<title>USA: Maine cities and towns urge property tax relief.</title>
<headline>Maine cities and towns urge property tax relief.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine's cities and towns, saying they pay some of the highest property taxes in the country, called for the state legislature to consider reforms that would cut their taxes and spread the burden more evenly.</p>
<p>The Maine Municipal Association Convention, a yearly gathering, said it wants the property tax system shifted to one that would be based on the ability to pay, like income taxes.</p>
<p>In 1995, property taxes in Maine produced more than $1 billion of revenues.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
